  "verdict": "salvageable",
  "summary": "The candidate is structurally coherent and contains real frontend implementation for the upload flow, not just scaffolding. It covers the main UI behaviors for selection, client-side validation, upload success, and 401/403 handling. However, it does not fully satisfy REQ-004 as written because the required browser smoke is not present; the emitted tests are jsdom component/integration tests only, and redirect behavior is proven through injected navigator callbacks rather than real routing/navigation. Docs and CI metadata overstate this as acceptance-complete.",
  "scope_fidelity": {
    "status": "partial",
    "notes": [
      "Core REQ-004 flow is implemented: Italian upload page, drag-and-drop, file picker input, client validation, success state, and next-action link.",
